       The Linux implementation of mandatory locking is subject to race condi‐
       tions which render it unreliable: a wwrriittee(2) call that overlaps with  a
       lock  may  modify  data after the mandatory lock is acquired; a rreeaadd(2)
       call that overlaps with a lock may detect changes  to  data  that  were
       made only after a write lock was acquired.  Similar races exist between
       mandatory  locks  and  mmmmaapp(2).  It is therefore inadvisable to rely on
       mandatory locking.

